      "text_raw": "As an exercise, let us try to\ncalculate the equivalent\ninput noise voltage of a\nMOST biased at 65 mA.\nOnly thermal noise is taken\ninto account and the layout\nis such that all Gate and\nBulk resistances can be\nignored. The expression is\nrepeated in this slide. A\ntransistor with 65 mA cur-\nrent, generates a transcon-\nductance of g =0.65 mS\nm\n(if V −V =0.2 V is\nGS T\nchosen). The noise resis-\ntance 2/3/g is then about\nm\n1 kV. The equivalent input noise voltage is therefore 4 nV /√Hz.\nRMS",
      "text": "As an exercise, let us try to calculate the equivalent input noise voltage of a MOST biased at 65 mA. Only thermal noise is taken into account and the layout is such that all Gate and Bulk resistances can be ignored. The expression is repeated in this slide. A transistor with 65 mA current, generates a transconductance of g =0.65 mS m (if V −V =0.2 V is GS T chosen). The noise resistance 2/3/g is then about m 1 kV. The equivalent input noise voltage is therefore 4 nV /√Hz. RMS"
